# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# GitHub Pages ignores this file (Jekyll skips underscore-prefixed paths), so it
# is safe to keep in the repo alongside the pages it serves.
#
# The site used to live at libertypictures.github.io/pg/, and the admin still
# generates some /pg/-shaped links. Anything under /pg/ folds onto the matching
# path at the site root, so no old link 404s — a 301 so search engines
# consolidate on the branded domain too.
/pg/*        /:splat        301

# The pay page is a directory (/pay/), but one admin template linked pay.html.
# Fold it so that link can never 404.
/pay.html    /pay/          301

# Bare /pay should land on the directory listing, not a 404.
/pay         /pay/          301
